    "description": "Scoop Capacity: Volumetric capacity 340 ml (12 oz) &middot; Length 210mm &middot; Solid cast food-grade aluminium &middot; Bulk carton quantities for commercial bars, ice machines and grain bins. Aluminium Scoop Specifications Volumetric Capacity 340 ml (12 oz) Total Overall Length 210mm Material Construction Seamless one-piece polished cast aluminium alloy Handle Ergonomics Contoured grip with anti-slip finger grooves and thumb rest Recommended Applications Commercial bar ice wells, dry ingredient bins (flour/sugar), and pet food packaging The 210mm aluminium ice scoop is a one-piece, food-grade scoop for bar ice wells and busy beverage stations. Spun from a single sheet of aluminium with no seams or welds, there is nowhere for ice, sugar or powder residue to lodge, which makes it quick to rinse clean and easy to keep hygienic between services. Guides &amp; resources Ice Cream Parlour Supplies for Sampling and Service Wholesale Packaging and Catering Supplies in South Africa Restaurant Opening Procurement Checklist Stainless Steel Food Service Equipment Guide Catering Equipment for Events: From Prep to Service Ice Scoops for Catering Key features One-piece food-grade aluminium, no seams to trap residue Lightweight with a comfortable grip for repeated scooping Will not rust, chip or crack like plastic scoops Suitable for ice, dry goods, flour, sugar, grains and powders Easy to sanitise; dishwasher friendly Specifications Overall length: 210mm Material: one-piece food-grade aluminium Construction: seamless spun body - no welds or joins Suitable for: ice, flour, sugar, grains and powders Care: dishwasher friendly Choosing the right size Smaller scoops (165-220mm) suit bar service, garnish stations and dosing smaller containers; mid sizes (250-270mm) are the all-round choice for ice wells and dry stores; the 350mm and 400mm scoops move bulk ice and ingredients fast in high-volume kitchens, butcheries and production lines. Ice scoop size guide Aluminium scoops are sized by overall length. As a rule of thumb, the longer the scoop, the larger the bowl capacity and the faster you can move ice or dry goods. This guide compares the full Mitrend range: Length Best suited for 165mm Garnish stations, spice bins and small bar wells 180mm Cocktail bars and coffee stations 210mm Dry goods dispensing and mid-size ice wells 250mm All-round kitchen and dry store use 270mm Busy ice wells and self-service stations 400mm Bulk ice machines, flour and grain bins 400mm heavy-duty High-volume storage and production kitchens Why aluminium? Aluminium is the industry standard for ice and dry-goods scoops because it is light enough for repeated one-handed use, will not rust, chip or crack like plastic alternatives, and transfers cold quickly so ice does not clump against the bowl. A one-piece spun construction means there are no seams, welds or rivets where bacteria can collect - an important consideration for HACCP-run kitchens. Care and cleaning Wash in warm soapy water or a commercial dishwasher and dry promptly. Avoid caustic or high-alkaline detergents, which can discolour aluminium over time - the discolouration is cosmetic and does not affect food safety. Store the scoop outside the ice bin, on a hook or in a scoop holder, to comply with food-safety best practice. Ordering and related products Sold individually with wholesale carton pricing available. Order online or request a bulk quote for multi-unit pricing."
